# DTF tier manifest: admin-hidden-nav  (artifact-keeper#4574, fixed by #4575)
# Profile-set: filesystem / single. The feature lives entirely in the
# management API and the key/value system_settings table, ahead of any storage
# backend, so the oracle is pure HTTP plus direct reads and writes of the DB.
#
# THE FEATURE (#4574)
# The web sidebar lists every feature and most instances use a few. #4575 adds
# hidden_nav_items to the runtime settings endpoint (GET/PATCH
# /api/v1/admin/settings/system), stores it in system_settings under
# ui.hidden_nav_items, audits each write as SETTING_CHANGED with
# details {setting, from, to}, and publishes it to every caller, anonymous
# included (guests see the sidebar too), as ui.hidden_nav_items on
# GET /api/v1/system/config.
# The identifiers are OPAQUE to the server (the web UI sends route paths such
# as /peers). The server checks shape only: 1-128 bytes of ASCII letters,
# digits, '/', '-', '_', '.', at most 200 entries; it trims, sorts and
# de-duplicates; one bad entry refuses the whole request (400) before anything
# is written. There is no allowed set and no un-hideable entry on the server.
# A missing, unreadable or malformed stored value reads as an empty list.
#
# THE PRIMITIVES
#   store     admin PATCH ["/webhooks","/peers","/peers"," /plugins "]
#             fixed:  200 ["/peers","/plugins","/webhooks"], admin GET and the
#                     DB row agree, guest_access_enabled untouched.
#             1.11.3: 422 unknown field `hidden_nav_items`.
#   publish   anonymous and non-admin GET /system/config.
#             fixed:  ui.hidden_nav_items is the stored list.
#             1.11.3: no ui key.
#   refuse    "not allowed", "", "<script>", a 129-byte id, 201 entries, and a
#             valid guest flag beside an invalid list.
#             fixed:  400 naming hidden_nav_items, stored list unchanged.
#             1.11.3: 422.
#   audit     audit_log SETTING_CHANGED rows with details.setting =
#             ui.hidden_nav_items: one per accepted write (user = the admin,
#             from [] to the list), none for the refused ones.
#   malformed {"not":"a list"}, "/peers", [1,2] and JSON null written straight
#             into system_settings.
#             fixed:  admin GET and /system/config answer 200 with [].
#             1.11.3: no such field (null).
#
# THE GATES
#   (FIX)      the primitives above, RED on 1.11.3.
#   (CONTROL)  must hold on BOTH images: /system/config keeps exactly its four
#              pre-#4575 keys (auth, demo_mode, guest_access_enabled,
#              max_upload_size_bytes) apart from ui, and their values are the
#              same before and after the navigation writes; the admin settings
#              read is refused to a non-admin (403/404) and to anonymous; a
#              non-admin or anonymous PATCH is refused and writes no row; the
#              guest-access PATCH still round-trips.
#
# RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED=false: ~50 back-to-back calls.
PROFILES="storage.filesystem"
ORACLE="oracle.sh"
RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED="false"
